  <section id="chto-eto">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>The tarsal tunnel lies behind the inner ankle and is covered by a dense ligament. The tibial nerve, artery, veins and tendons pass through it into the foot. The nerve supplies sensation to the sole and controls the small muscles of the foot.</p>
    <NerveMap limb="leg" focus="tarsal" lang="en" />
    <h3>Causes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>flat feet and an inward-rolling foot;</li>
      <li>ankle injuries and fractures and the swelling after them;</li>
      <li>enlarged veins, cysts, bony spurs in the canal;</li>
      <li>tight shoes, long standing;</li>
      <li>swelling with joint disease or diabetes.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="simptomy">
    <h2>Symptoms</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>burning, tingling and numbness of the sole and toes;</li>
      <li>symptoms worsen when walking, standing for long, in the evening and at night;</li>
      <li>pain behind the inner ankle radiating into the foot when this spot is tapped;</li>
      <li>in advanced cases — weakness of the small foot muscles.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="diagnostika">
    <h2>Diagnosis</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Nerve conduction study</strong> — confirms nerve compression and distinguishes it from polyneuropathy.</li>
      <li><strong>Ankle ultrasound or MRI</strong> — looks for the cause: cysts, veins, bony spurs.</li>
      <li>Blood sugar and vitamin tests — so as not to miss polyneuropathy.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="lechenie">
    <h2>Treatment</h2>
    <p><strong>Without surgery</strong> — orthotic insoles for flat feet, comfortable shoes, less load, exercise therapy. Medication and injections are prescribed by a doctor.</p>
    <p><strong>Surgery</strong> — division of the tarsal tunnel ligament and release of the nerve and its branches, removal of a cyst if present. It is considered when the diagnosis is confirmed by tests, the cause is found and non-surgical treatment does not help. After surgery the foot is spared from load for several weeks; stitches come out on day 10–14.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="srochno" slot="urgent">
    <h2>When to seek urgent help</h2>
    <div class="callout alert">
      <p>The foot has become cold, pale or bluish, with sudden pain and swelling of the calf — <strong>call emergency services immediately (112; 103 in Russia)</strong>: this may be a circulation problem or a blood clot.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
